\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces CPG assembly line in five sequential steps (order is arbitrary): (A) Four uncoupled interneurons, with Si3 neurons firing at a higher rate due to excitatory drive from Si1 neurons. (B) Si3 neurons provide fast excitatory drive to ipsilateral Si2 neurons. (C) Si2 neurons deliver inhibitory feedback onto Si3 neurons. (D) Reciprocally inhibitory synapses are activated between contralateral Si3 neurons. (E) Reciprocally inhibitory synapses are activated between contralateral Si2 neurons, along with gap junctions between Si3 neurons, which together generate stable fast network-level bursting in the swim CPG model of {\em  Dendronotus iris}.}}{7}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:group_fig5}{{7}{7}{CPG assembly line in five sequential steps (order is arbitrary): (A) Four uncoupled interneurons, with Si3 neurons firing at a higher rate due to excitatory drive from Si1 neurons. (B) Si3 neurons provide fast excitatory drive to ipsilateral Si2 neurons. (C) Si2 neurons deliver inhibitory feedback onto Si3 neurons. (D) Reciprocally inhibitory synapses are activated between contralateral Si3 neurons. (E) Reciprocally inhibitory synapses are activated between contralateral Si2 neurons, along with gap junctions between Si3 neurons, which together generate stable fast network-level bursting in the swim CPG model of {\em Dendronotus iris}}{figure.7}{}}
